# Project

2D physics ragdoll simulator in Unity 6000.5.8f1. Four models, do not mix
layers: human (stance and balance by muscles), bird (flap → lift on the
body), tree (recursive segments, spring, no muscles), and dog (quadruped
stance by muscles). A flock in scene is `BirdRig.Flock` (one body). The
human and the dog have no invisible "up" force.

The physics scene is built in code from `GameProcess.Start()`. No prefabs.
Seven saved scenes — do not mix Play Mode, so chats do not open the wrong
model in one Editor:

| Scene | Whose Play | What it spawns |
|---|---|---|
| `SampleScene` | 2D physics / stand | `humanCount = 1`, no birds, no trees, no dogs. **Do not touch.** |
| `Bird` | Bird / bird AI | `humanCount = 0`, `birdCount = 1`, `cameraFollowsBird`. Flat ground, no `LevelGenerator`. |
| `BirdFlock50` | bird AI flock | `humanCount = 0`, `birdCount = 50`, `birdDrive` wander. Flat ground, no `LevelGenerator`. |
| `Chicken` | ground bird | `humanCount = 0`, `birdCount = 5`, `birdKind` chicken, `birdDrive` wander. Flat ground. |
| `Tree` | plants | `humanCount = 0`, `birdCount = 0`, `treeCount = 1`. Flat ground, no `LevelGenerator`. |
| `Dog` | dog stance | `humanCount = 0`, `dogCount = 1`. Flat ground, no `LevelGenerator`. |
| `World` | levels / optimization | human + yard. `birdCount = 0`, `birdDrive` off, `treeCount = 0`, `dogCount = 0`. |

One Unity Editor and one `-Rebuild` for the project. Scenes split Play
eyes, not two solvers at once. Headless human: `run-trial.ps1` on
`SampleScene`, Editor not required. Bird on the stand: `-bird 1`, not
scene `World`.

## Layers (do not mix)

| Layer | Files |
|---|---|
| Boot | `GameProcess`, `GroundBuilder` |
| World | `LevelGenerator`, `StaticPlatform` |
| Body (human) | `Human`, `HumanSegment` |
| Body (bird) | `Bird` |
| Body (plant) | `PlantTree`, `TreeSpring`, `TreeDriver` |
| Body (dog) | `Dog` |
| Actuators | `Muscle`, `JointFriction` |
| Aero (bird) | `BirdFlight`, `BodyAero` |
| Sensors (human) | `VestibularSystem`, `CenterOfMassCalculator`, `BodyStateEstimator` |
| Sensors (bird) | `BirdSensors` |
| Control (human) | `BalanceController` |
| Control (bird) | `BirdController` |
| Control (dog) | `DogStanceController` |
| Intent | `MotionIntent`, `PlayerInputSource`, `StepPhaseDriver` |
| AI (every species) | rule `ai.mdc`; bird — `BirdDrive` writes `mode` / `SetFacing`; human — `MotionIntent` |
| Experiment | `HeadlessTrial`, `TrialRecorder`, `HeadlessBuild`, `GlobalHumanLogger` |

Sensors only read state and never apply forces.
Joint torques come from `Muscle` and `JointFriction`. Bird lift comes from
`BirdFlight` on the body (on while wings flap; zero without a flap). That
is not a muscle and not a joint motor.
Bird rules: `.cursor/rules/bird-physics.mdc`. Plants: `plant-physics.mdc`.
Dog: `dog-physics.mdc`. Every brain: `.cursor/rules/ai.mdc`.
The human headless stand does not spawn birds, trees, or dogs unless
the matching CLI flag is set.

